<title>USA: MAPCO sells reserves for $66 mln.</title>
<headline>MAPCO sells reserves for $66 mln.</headline>
<dateline>TULSA, Okla. 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>MAPCO Inc said Thursday it sold its natural gas liquids and condensate reserves in the West Panhandle Fields of Texas to Mesa Inc for $66 million.</p>
<p>The transaction, which was effective Jan 1, consists of natural gas liquids and condensate reserves with expected 1997 production of 850,000 barrels.</p>
<p>MAPCO said it will continue to provide pipeline transportation and fractionation services for Mesa's natural gas liquids production under a longterm contract.</p>
<p>In addition, MAPCO said it will purchase all of Mesa's natural gas liquids production to support its retail and wholesale marketing initiatives.</p>
</text>
